Manage a project's roles

Usage:
  patrol proj role [flags]
  patrol proj role [command]

Available Commands:
  add-group     Add a group claim to a project role
  add-policy    Add a policy to a project role
  create        Create a project role
  create-token  Create a project token
  delete        Delete a project role
  delete-token  Delete a project token
  get           Get the details of a specific role
  list          List all the roles in a project
  list-tokens   List tokens for a given role.
  remove-group  Remove a group claim from a role within a project
  remove-policy Remove a policy from a role within a project

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for role

Global Flags:
      --auth-token string               Authentication token; set this or the PATROL_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable
      --client-crt string               Client certificate file
      --client-crt-key string           Client certificate key file
      --cluster string                  The name of the kubeconfig cluster to use
      --config string                   Path to Patrol CD config (default "/home/patrol/.config/patrol/config")
      --context string                  The name of the kubeconfig context to use
      --controller-name string          Name of the Patrol CD Application controller; set this or the PATROL_APPLICATION_CONTROLLER_NAME environment variable when the controller's name label differs from the default, for example when installing via the Helm chart (default "patrol-application-controller")
      --core                            If set to true then CLI talks directly to Kubernetes instead of talking to Patrol CD API server
      --grpc-web                        Accepted for compatibility with Argo CD and ignored: Patrol CD serves JSON over HTTP, which works through any HTTP proxy.
      --grpc-web-root-path string       Root path of the Patrol CD server when it is served under a sub-path (Argo CD flag name kept for compatibility).
  -H, --header strings                  Sets additional header to all requests made by Patrol CD CLI. (Can be repeated multiple times to add multiple headers, also supports comma separated headers)
      --http-retry-max int              Maximum number of retries to establish http connection to Patrol CD server
      --insecure                        Skip server certificate and domain verification
      --insecure-skip-tls-verify        If true, the server's certificate will not be checked for validity. This will make your HTTPS connections insecure
      --kube-context string             Directs the command to the given kube-context
      --kubeconfig string               Path to a kube config. Only required if out-of-cluster
      --logformat string                Set the logging format. One of: json|text (default "json")
      --loglevel string                 Set the logging level. One of: debug|info|warn|error (default "info")
  -n, --namespace string                If present, the namespace scope for this CLI request
      --password string                 Password for basic authentication to the API server
      --patrol-context string           The name of the Patrol CD server context to use
      --plaintext                       Disable TLS
      --port-forward                    Connect to a random patrol-server port using port forwarding
      --port-forward-namespace string   Namespace name which should be used for port forwarding
      --prompts-enabled                 Force optional interactive prompts to be enabled or disabled, overriding local configuration. If not specified, the local configuration value will be used, which is false by default.
      --proxy-url string                If provided, this URL will be used to connect via proxy
      --repo-server-name string         Name of the Patrol CD Repo server; set this or the PATROL_REPO_SERVER_NAME environment variable when the server's name label differs from the default, for example when installing via the Helm chart (default "patrol-repo-server")
      --request-timeout string          The length of time to wait before giving up on a single server request. Non-zero values should contain a corresponding time unit (e.g. 1s, 2m, 3h). A value of zero means don't timeout requests. (default "0")
      --server string                   Patrol CD server address
      --server-crt string               Server certificate file
      --server-name string              Name of the Patrol CD API server; set this or the PATROL_SERVER_NAME environment variable when the server's name label differs from the default, for example when installing via the Helm chart (default "patrol-server")
      --token string                    Bearer token for authentication to the API server
      --user string                     The name of the kubeconfig user to use
      --username string                 Username for basic authentication to the API server

Use "patrol proj role [command] --help" for more information about a command.
